WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:04.259
I've told people to learn to use a
schedule and people often hate schedules

00:00:04.259 --> 00:00:07.730
because they act as their own tyrants
right they say we have to do this

00:00:07.730 --> 00:00:11.670
unpleasant thing and then here's another
unpleasant thing you have to do and then

00:00:11.670 --> 00:00:15.269
you have to do this unpleasant thing and
you do that for about three days and you

00:00:15.269 --> 00:00:18.869
think Oh tell with this I'm not doing
that you know and you fall off the wagon

00:00:18.869 --> 00:00:23.340
that isn't what you're supposed to do
with the schedule you're supposed to use

00:00:23.340 --> 00:00:27.480
it to design the days that you would
like to have if you were taking care of

00:00:27.480 --> 00:00:31.820
yourself and so some of that is you know
you wake up in the morning and you think

00:00:31.820 --> 00:00:37.050
here's five things I have to do that if
I don't do my life will be worse it's

00:00:37.050 --> 00:00:41.820
like paying bills for example or taking
out the garbage it's like you have to do

00:00:41.820 --> 00:00:44.850
those because otherwise things
degenerate so you got to put some of

00:00:44.850 --> 00:00:48.510
those in the schedule because otherwise
tomorrow is worse than today and that's

00:00:48.510 --> 00:00:53.789
a bad trajectory but you also want to
build in things you know you gotta act

00:00:53.789 --> 00:00:57.750
in some sense like you're dealing with a
relatively recalcitrant nine year old

00:00:57.750 --> 00:01:01.829
it's like so well here are some things
you have to do but here's some things

00:01:01.829 --> 00:01:06.390
that if you do you could reward yourself
with and if you get the balance there

00:01:06.390 --> 00:01:10.770
between obligation and reward right then
you'll find that you're motivated to do

00:01:10.770 --> 00:01:13.560
the things and that's what you want to
do you want to do that so it's

00:01:13.560 --> 00:01:17.729
sustainable across days and weeks and
months and so you got to you got to

00:01:17.729 --> 00:01:23.729
treat yourself like a good boss would
treat a valued employee and not like a

00:01:23.729 --> 00:01:28.320
tyrant would treat a slave because the
slave will rebel and you know people say

00:01:28.320 --> 00:01:33.780
well I don't follow through on my plans
it's like well eh they're probably not

00:01:33.780 --> 00:01:37.770
very well formulated and maybe you're
doing them because of an external moral

00:01:37.770 --> 00:01:42.869
obligation or something not really your
plans right and B you're acting like a

00:01:42.869 --> 00:01:47.490
tyrant and a slave and that's a bad
relationship to have with yourself so

00:01:47.490 --> 00:01:52.619
you you want to treat yourself with some
well the same way that's the Golden Rule

00:01:52.619 --> 00:01:57.240
write it treat yourself as you would
treat other people as you would have

00:01:57.240 --> 00:02:01.530
them sorry treat other people as you
would like to be treated it works both

00:02:01.530 --> 00:02:04.530
ways
you also treat yourself like you treat

00:02:04.530 --> 00:02:08.580
other people properly so that's a
necessary thing and often people don't

00:02:08.580 --> 00:02:11.000
do that

